    The King Edward was the world's first commercial turbine passenger steamer and served the Greenock to Campbeltown run, commanded by Captain Fowler. \n
    During the First World War she mostly served transporting troops to France, but on at least one trip went to Arkhangelsk (Archangel) in northern Russia.\n
